      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m torn on whether or not we should add labels to these. Initially I thought yes, but then I realized it got complicated if this was called with a graphite-backed image that may or may not be compatible with the required properties, but otherwise had a label. Do we use the new label if we end up not copying?\n\nAnd when it\u0027s a raster-backed image or other lazy image, the labels are already fairly informative as to what\u0027s inside them. Adding a custom label would let you attach an asset ID or filename, but that doesn\u0027t seem as valuable when debugging as SkSurface custom labels.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 250,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 250,
        "endChar": 38
